cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this atlas or its walkthroughs in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: book
title: "Coursework · A Capstone Atlas"
subtitle: "Learning Systems Thinking through Capstone Projects"
abstract: >-
  A bilingual (Chinese/English) atlas of 34 computer-science capstone
  assignments drawn from 14 universities. Twenty-two are original walkthroughs
  written for this project; twelve are real course repositories kept as git
  submodules, each paired with an independent reference implementation that
  passes the original tests. Every number quoted in the book comes from a real
  run, and the code that produced it is in the repository.
authors:
  - name: "polarours"
    website: "https://github.com/polarours"
repository-code: "https://github.com/polarours/Coursework"
url: "https://polarours.github.io/Coursework/"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
keywords:
  - computer science education
  - capstone projects
  - systems programming
  - distributed systems
  - algorithms and data structures
  - bilingual textbook
  - reproducible coursework
